 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Popcorn, crackers, and sandwich pieces like dry cured prosciutto or french salt beef that are kept in a box in the kitchen. Pasta is fine without a fridge for few hours. Fresh cut and wrapped in moist towels, it's fine for several days. If it' been more than a morning, get new cut ones. You can skip it completely, or get a pre cut one. Put it on plate and wrap it well. A thin layer of condensation won't hurt it. Fresh fruit and sandwich spreads don't need a fridge. A box of sandwich bits is also fine.",
